  "title": "The Crowded Hash Locker",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "computing/data",
  "premise": "A librarian wants fast storage lookup, but two book keys map to the same locker. A visible collision list retains both books and a full-key check retrieves the requested one.",
  "hook": "Two keys, one locker: did a book disappear?",
  "visible_action": "Key cards pass through a toy modulo machine; colliding cards stack in one bucket and are compared individually.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Hash collisions require an explicit resolution and key-checking strategy.",
  "gate": "Use a toy hash table; do not conflate indexing hashes with cryptographic security.",
